---
import FaqList from "../../components/FaqList.astro";
import AudienceLayout from "../../layouts/AudienceLayout.astro";
---

<AudienceLayout
	title="Other professionals"
	lead="Information for health, early help, youth justice and voluntary sector partners supporting children in care in Rotherham."
	description="Information for health, early help, virtual partners and anyone supporting a child in care."
	accent="var(--rvs-audience-other)"
>
	<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">How we work with partners</h2>
	<p class="govuk-body">
		Children in care are supported by many services. The Virtual School focuses only on education,
		but we cannot do that well in isolation. We work with health, early help, youth justice,
		housing and the voluntary sector to make sure the support around a child joins up.
	</p>

	<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Health and emotional wellbeing</h2>
	<p class="govuk-body">
		Children in care have a statutory health assessment, and emotional wellbeing is often the
		biggest barrier to learning. If you are working with a child on mental health, and it is
		affecting their school life, tell us — we can make sure the school puts the right adjustments
		in place.
	</p>

	<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Early help and family support</h2>
	<p class="govuk-body">
		Where a child is on a child in need or child protection plan, or in kinship care, the Virtual
		School's role is different but the education focus still matters. We can advise on
		attendance, admissions and support in school.
	</p>

	<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Sharing information</h2>
	<p class="govuk-body">
		We will share information with you where it is necessary to support a child's education, in
		line with our <a class="govuk-link" href="/privacy-cookies/">privacy notice</a>. Please
		contact the team rather than individual staff where a request relates to more than one child.
	</p>

	<FaqList audience="professionals" />
</AudienceLayout>
